# Force LF line endings on shell scripts regardless of the cloning
# platform's line-ending settings. Without this, a Windows clone with
# git's default `core.autocrlf` behaviour can check these out with CRLF
# endings, and setup.sh -- the first thing the quickstart tells a new
# user to run -- fails immediately with `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M`,
# on exactly the platform this project most needs to prove it works on.
*.sh text eol=lf
